<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greenland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kalaallit Nunaat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Greenland is the world's largest island, lying between the North Atlantic and Arctic oceans, and an autonomous territory of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. Norse settlers led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erik-the-red">Erik the Red</a> founded colonies there around 985, which accepted Norwegian rule in 1261 but died out in the 15th century. Danish-Norwegian colonisation resumed in 1721; Greenland gained home rule in 1979 and self-government in 2009. Most of its people are <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inuit">Inuit</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greenland.jpg" alt="Greenland" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeffrey Connell (IceKarma) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Greenland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
